The user is asking for a single-page HTML presentation that displays the bilingual content side by side (English and Chinese) in `index.html`. CSS and JavaScript should be embedded, no external resources.

Let me plan:
- A single HTML file with embedded CSS/JS
- Content: the bilingual sky.md content (English from sky.md, Chinese from sky2.md)
- Side-by-side layout: English on the left, Chinese on the right, for each section
- Sections: Intro, 3-year-old, High schooler, Physics PhD, Further Reading
- The physics PhD section contains LaTeX math. External resources (like MathJax) are not allowed. So the math has to be rendered some other way. Options:
  1. Use HTML/CSS to render the formulas (e.g., styled fractions with sub/sup tags)
  2. Use Unicode math symbols

The two main equations are:
1. dσ/dΩ = (k⁴/(4πε₀²)) |n̂ · α · k̂|²
2. σ = (8π³/3) (α²/λ⁴) · 1/(4πε₀)² ∝ 1/λ⁴

These can be written in HTML with fraction styling (a span with a border-top for the fraction line), or more simply with a linearized representation like "dσ/dΩ = k⁴/(4πε₀²) |n̂·α·k̂|²".

For a clean presentation, I can make a simple fraction component:
```html
<span class="frac"><span class="num">dσ</span><span class="den">dΩ</span></span>
```
with CSS:
```css
.frac { display: inline-flex; flex-direction: column; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; }
.frac .num { border-bottom: 1px solid; padding: 0 2px; }
```

This should look nice enough.

Features to include:
- Header with title (bilingual)
- Three "audience" sections, each as a card with a 2-column layout (English | Chinese)
- Responsive: stack vertically on narrow screens
- Maybe a nav / section switcher with a bit of JS? "Clean and simple" is requested, but the JS is embedded — I should include at least some JS to make it functional. Options:
  - A button to toggle sections (like slides: intro, toddler, teen, PhD) — this makes it more of a "presentation"
  - Or keyboard navigation between sections
  - Section navigation at the top, plus arrow keys

Since it says "presentation," having section navigation (buttons/tabs to jump between the 3 audience levels) would be nice. A "presentation" might mean slideshow-style. Let me go with this:
- All sections visible on the page (single page), with sticky nav pills at the top for scrolling to each section
- Side-by-side columns for each section
- Maybe a subtle JS: scroll-spy highlighting of nav, plus a toggle to collapse the math?

Keep it clean: header, nav pills (scroll to section, active highlighting via IntersectionObserver or scroll), 3 content cards each with EN | ZH columns, footer.

Actually, as a "presentation," slide mode might be better: show one section at a time, navigate with buttons/arrow keys. But "display this bilingual content side by side" suggests showing the two languages side by side — that's about EN/CH columns, not slides.

